import json, os
ROOT=os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)),'../../../../..'))
ALL=[n['chainId'] for n in json.load(open(os.path.join(ROOT,'research/network-risk/state/networks.json')))['networks']]
N0="No property of a chain or of a token is involved, so the result is the same on all 21 networks."
NA10="The only reliance is A10, the EVM semantics of the bit and arithmetic opcodes. The opcode vector probes recorded in state/cleared.json found these equal to Ethereum on all 21 networks, and this unit ran no new chain query for it."
NC="The reliance is on the solc 0.8.26 via-IR build named in foundry.toml and on no chain property, so it is the same on all 21 networks. No compiler is installed here, so the bytecode was not inspected."
NA1="The reliance is A1: transient storage must be private to the PoolManager, roll back with a reverted frame and be empty at the start of each transaction. The per network status of A1 is the one recorded in state/cleared.json by the transient storage units, and this unit ran no new chain query for it."
cleared=[]
def C(check,result,source,lens='L1'):
    cleared.append({'chainIds':ALL,'lens':lens,'check':check,'result':result,'source':source})

# ---------------- Certora ----------------
C("Certora M-01 (medium): assembly blocks marked memory-safe wrote past the scratch space, which lets the optimizer corrupt code.",
  "Closed in the text. Every assembly block in src outside src/test writes only to bytes 0x00 to 0x3f or to memory at and after the free pointer: the position hash uses mload(0x40) and zeroes its three words (src/libraries/Position.sol:54-66), the two argument reverts use the free pointer (src/libraries/CustomRevert.sol:49-79), the token transfer writes 68 bytes at the free pointer and zeroes them (src/types/Currency.sol:55-80), flipTick puts its error at the free pointer and its hash input in scratch (src/libraries/TickBitmap.sol:57-70), and callHook moves the free pointer past the copied return data (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:140-149). "+NC,
  "src/libraries/Position.sol:54")
C("Certora L-01 (low, acknowledged, not fixed): after a swap the price can never return to MIN_SQRT_PRICE, so liquidity in the lowest price step is usable once.",
  "Unchanged and intended. A zeroForOne limit equal to MIN_SQRT_PRICE is rejected (src/libraries/Pool.sol:328-330). The same comparison is what keeps slot0.tick from reaching MIN_TICK - 1, which Spearbit 5.4.9 asks for, so relaxing it as Certora proposed would reopen that item. The effect is a pool that cannot trade in its last price step and no funds move. "+N0,
  "src/libraries/Pool.sol:328")
C("Certora L-02 (low): an attacker fills liquidityGross of chosen ticks to the per tick cap so that later deposits that use those ticks revert.",
  "Nothing in src closes it and the report records documentation as the fix. The cap is enforced at src/libraries/Pool.sol:165-173 and computed at Pool.sol:565-582. The hazard is already in the ledger as F-038 for all 21 networks and this unit adds no new fact to it. "+N0,
  "src/libraries/Pool.sol:165")
C("Certora L-03 (low, impact high): assembly reads values of narrow types as full words, so dirty upper bits could change results.",
  "Closed. Each assembly use of a narrow value masks or sign extends it first: TickBitmap.sol:20-21, 38-39 and 54-55, TickMath.sol:61, SqrtPriceMath.sol:62, 110, 137-138, 166-167, 198 and 217, SwapMath.sol:31-33, ProtocolFeeLibrary.sol:28-29 and 41-42, LiquidityMath.sol:12, Pool.sol:552-554 and 576, CurrencyDelta.sol:12-13, CurrencyReserves.sol:29, CustomRevert.sol:25-76, Currency.sol:61, Slot0.sol:68-91. A scan of every hex literal in src found each address mask with 40 hex digits and each 128 bit mask with 32 (cycles/007/core-code-audit-walk-b.work/consts_check.out). Two values leave assembly unmasked, the bytes4 of ParseBytes.parseSelector and the uint24 of parseFee (src/libraries/ParseBytes.sol:9-21). They are used in a comparison (Hooks.sol:152) and in a memory struct field (PoolManager.sol:209-215), where the compiler cleans them. "+NA10,
  "src/libraries/ParseBytes.sol:9")
C("Certora I-01 (informational, partial fix): any contract called during an unlock can open a nonzero delta for itself and make the whole unlock revert.",
  "Not closed, by design. unlock reverts when any delta is open (src/PoolManager.sol:112) and take, mint and a swap can be called by any address while the flag is set (PoolManager.sol:96-99). The outcome is a revert of the caller's own transaction, so it fails closed and no funds move. The report links its partial fix only by pull request number, and I could not tell from the report text which statement of src it refers to. "+NA1,
  "src/PoolManager.sol:112")
C("Certora I-02 (informational): mint and burn took a uint256 id whose upper 96 bits were ignored for the currency and kept for the claim, so one currency had 2^96 claim ids.",
  "Closed. mint and burn convert the id to a Currency first and pass currency.toId() to _mint and _burnFrom, so the claim id always has zero upper bits (src/PoolManager.sol:324-327 and 333-335, src/types/Currency.sol:110-118). "+N0,
  "src/PoolManager.sol:324")
C("Certora I-03 (informational) and ABDK CVF-15 and CVF-16 (major): the array forms of extsload and exttload assumed the ABI offset of the array is 0x20 and could misread calldata.",
  "Closed. Both functions take the array as bytes32[] calldata and use slots.offset and slots.length, which the compiler derives from the offset word, and they write the 0x20 return offset themselves (src/Extsload.sol:42-63, src/Exttload.sol:18-39). They are view functions and move no funds (A11). "+NC,
  "src/Extsload.sol:42")
C("Certora formal properties P-01 to P-07 and the library properties: deltas are zero when locked, initialization sets a valid price once, only modifyLiquidity changes a position and only for msg.sender, fees stay within their caps, flipTick flips one bit.",
  "The text has each property. The delta counter changes only in _accountDelta and only when a delta becomes or stops being zero (src/PoolManager.sol:368-378), and unlock checks it before closing the lock (PoolManager.sol:112-113). initialize rejects a second call and validates the price (Pool.sol:100-107, TickMath.sol:127-129). The position owner is msg.sender (PoolManager.sol:161). LP fees are validated at LPFeeLibrary.sol:43-55, PoolManager.sol:343 and Pool.sol:303-305, protocol fees at ProtocolFees.sol:37. The report marks TickSqrtPriceStrongCorrelation as violated, which is Certora M-02 and is carried in the donation finding of this file. P-01 relies on A1. "+NA1,
  "src/PoolManager.sol:368")

# ---------------- Spearbit ----------------
C("Spearbit 5.2.1 (low): tickSpacingToMaxLiquidityPerTick compressed MIN_TICK toward zero, so the tick count was off by one.",
  "Closed. The function subtracts one when MIN_TICK is not a multiple of the spacing (src/libraries/Pool.sol:576-580). A transcription matched floor compression for every spacing from 1 to 32767 (cycles/007/core-code-audit-walk-b.work/math_model.out). "+NA10,
  "src/libraries/Pool.sol:577")
C("Spearbit 5.2.2 (low, partly fixed by comments): getSqrtPriceAtTick mixes rounding directions and four of its multipliers differ by one from the rounded up value.",
  "Unchanged by decision and harmless. I recomputed 2^128 / sqrt(1.0001)^(2^i) at 400 digits: all 20 multipliers in src/libraries/TickMath.sol:80-100 are the nearest integers, and the four that Spearbit lists (i = 0, 12, 17, 19) are the ones where nearest and rounded up differ. A full sweep of all 1,774,545 ticks found the function strictly increasing, with getTickAtSqrtPrice returning t at the price of t and t - 1 one unit below it, and MIN_SQRT_PRICE and MAX_SQRT_PRICE equal to the outputs at the two end ticks (cycles/007/core-code-audit-walk-b.work/math_model.out). "+NA10,
  "src/libraries/TickMath.sol:80")
C("Spearbit 5.2.3 (low) and ABDK CVF-97 (minor): the two error bound constants of getTickAtSqrtPrice are not exact.",
  "No wrong tick results from them. The constants at src/libraries/TickMath.sol:225-233 give the correct tick on both sides of every tick boundary in the full sweep above, and prices outside [MIN_SQRT_PRICE, MAX_SQRT_PRICE) revert (TickMath.sol:127-129). "+NA10,
  "src/libraries/TickMath.sol:228")
C("Spearbit 5.2.4 (low, acknowledged) and 5.4.13 (informational, acknowledged): updateDynamicLPFee and collectProtocolFees emit no event of their own.",
  "Unchanged (src/PoolManager.sol:339-346, src/ProtocolFees.sol:44-57). This limits monitoring and moves no funds. "+N0,
  "src/PoolManager.sol:339")
C("Spearbit 5.2.5 (low, no response recorded): bubbleUpAndRevertWith copies return data of any size and pads the copy with whatever the memory held.",
  "Nothing in src bounds the copy (src/libraries/CustomRevert.sol:83-119), and callHook also copies the full return data of a successful hook call (src/libraries/Hooks.sol:140-149). The wrapped revert runs only after a native transfer, token transfer or hook call has already failed (Currency.sol:51-53 and 82-86, Hooks.sol:137), so the transaction reverts either way, and a hook that returns very large data can only stop actions in its own pool. The padding bytes can expose stale memory in the revert data, which holds no secret, because the contract keeps none: all of its storage and transient storage is public through extsload and exttload (A11). Gas for memory growth is a chain property (A9, A10), and a higher price for it makes the same call fail earlier. No path treats the failed call as a success.",
  "src/libraries/CustomRevert.sol:83")
C("Spearbit 5.3.1, 5.3.2, 5.3.5, 5.3.8, 5.3.9, 5.3.10 and 5.3.11 (gas, fixed): simpler upcast, constant length in toId, plain read of liquidityGross, unchecked negation in clear, plain tick assignment, simpleMulDiv for fee growth, shorter bitmap mask.",
  "Each change is present and keeps the value it replaced: SqrtPriceMath.sol:241, PoolId.sol:14, Pool.sol:526, PoolManager.sol:316-318 (amountDelta is not negative because SafeCast.sol:56-59 rejects 2^127 and above), Pool.sol:430-432, Pool.sol:404-405 and 474-477, TickBitmap.sol:97. simpleMulDiv multiplies without an overflow check (UnsafeMath.sol:24-28). In donate the amount is below 2^127 because the cast at Pool.sol:471 runs first, and in swap a step fee of 2^127 or more makes the final casts at Pool.sol:455-459 revert, so the code enforces the bound itself and does not rely on a token having a supply below 2^128. "+N0,
  "src/libraries/Pool.sol:404")
C("Spearbit 5.3.3 and 5.3.6 (gas, not applied) and 5.3.7 (gas, other change applied): reuse of the cached price, inlining msg.sender in _burnFrom, and the scratch space read in _fetchProtocolFee.",
  "The first two were declined and the text is unchanged (Pool.sol:322-338, ERC6909Claims.sol:13-22). _fetchProtocolFee no longer exists: the PoolManager makes no call to the fee controller, and the controller pushes a fee with setProtocolFee (src/ProtocolFees.sol:35-41). That removes the call whose return data the item and ABDK CVF-17 and CVF-174 describe. "+N0,
  "src/ProtocolFees.sol:35")
C("Spearbit 5.3.4 (gas, fixed) with 5.2.1: remove the multiply and divide by tickSpacing in tickSpacingToMaxLiquidityPerTick.",
  "Present, together with the rounding correction of 5.2.1 (src/libraries/Pool.sol:572-581). Verified for all spacings as stated under 5.2.1. "+NA10,
  "src/libraries/Pool.sol:572")
C("Spearbit 5.3.12 (gas, fixed) and ABDK CVF-29 and CVF-30 (moderate): BitMath was replaced by table lookups, and two bytes of the most significant bit table are never read.",
  "The table at src/libraries/BitMath.sol:22-23 is the value the report suggests, with the two unused bytes set to zero. A transcription of both functions returned the right index for every bit position from 0 to 255 with 400 random fillings each (cycles/007/core-code-audit-walk-b.work/math_model.out). Both functions require a nonzero input (BitMath.sol:13 and 32). "+NA10,
  "src/libraries/BitMath.sol:22")
C("Spearbit 5.4.1, 5.4.3, 5.4.5, 5.4.6, 5.4.12, 5.4.16 and 5.4.17 (informational): pragma convention, test constant comments, an unused constant, a needless unchecked block, unused named returns, a duplicate currency helper, comment wording.",
  "No fund effect. The unused offset is commented out (StateLibrary.sol:16), divRoundingUp has no unchecked block (UnsafeMath.sol:12-16), settle and settleFor return unnamed values (PoolManager.sol:300-307) and only isAddressZero remains (Currency.sol:106-108). One comment change of 5.4.17 is not in the text: IPoolManager.sol:111 still names only initialize and updateDynamicLPFee as callable without an unlock, while sync has no lock modifier (PoolManager.sol:279). That is the second item of F-006. "+N0,
  "src/interfaces/IPoolManager.sol:111")
C("Spearbit 5.4.2 and 5.4.4 (informational) and ABDK CVF-6 (major): in an exact input step that does not reach the target, amountIn was recomputed and the fee was taken as an unchecked difference that relied on distant code.",
  "Closed locally. amountIn is set to amountRemainingLessFee, which is mulDiv of the remaining amount by a factor of at most one, so the subtraction at src/libraries/SwapMath.sol:82 cannot underflow (SwapMath.sol:64-65 and 77). At a 100 percent fee both amountIn and the fee of a completed step are zero, as the comment at SwapMath.sol:73 says. "+N0,
  "src/libraries/SwapMath.sol:77")
C("Spearbit 5.4.7 (informational, custom errors dropped for code size) and ABDK CVF-48, CVF-49 and CVF-50 (moderate): balances, allowances and accrued protocol fees are protected only by checked subtraction.",
  "Still so, and sufficient. The subtractions at src/ERC6909.sol:26, 38, 41 and 86, src/ERC6909Claims.sol:18 and src/ProtocolFees.sol:55 are outside any unchecked block. mint calls _mint from inside an unchecked block (PoolManager.sol:323-328), and an unchecked block does not extend into called functions, so the addition at ERC6909.sol:80 stays checked. "+NC,
  "src/ERC6909.sol:26")
C("Spearbit 5.4.8 (informational) and ABDK CVF-37 (moderate): getSqrtPriceAtTick assumes MIN_TICK equals minus MAX_TICK.",
  "Holds by the constants: MIN_TICK is -887272 and MAX_TICK is 887272 (src/libraries/TickMath.sol:20-23) and the bound check uses the absolute value (TickMath.sol:70). "+N0,
  "src/libraries/TickMath.sol:70")
C("Spearbit 5.4.9 (informational, addressed): the next tick is clipped off the spacing grid and slot0.tick could fall to MIN_TICK - 1.",
  "Closed for the second part. A zeroForOne limit must be above MIN_SQRT_PRICE (src/libraries/Pool.sol:328-330), the step target is the larger of the next tick price and the limit (SwapMath.sol:25-36), so a step never ends on the price of MIN_TICK and the decrement at Pool.sol:431 never starts from MIN_TICK. A clipped tick below MIN_TICK cannot be initialized because checkTicks rejects it (Pool.sol:94-98). slot0.tick off the grid is expected. "+N0,
  "src/libraries/Pool.sol:328")
C("Spearbit 5.4.10 (informational) and ABDK CVF-8 (major): the unchecked blocks of Pool.swap, among them the protocol fee product that ABDK calls a phantom overflow.",
  "Safe as written. The total input of a swap passes through toInt128 at src/libraries/Pool.sol:455-459 and, for exact output, through the checked subtraction at Pool.sol:375, so any step with amountIn + feeAmount of 2^127 or more ends in a revert and the product with a protocol fee of at most 1000 at Pool.sol:393 cannot wrap in a swap that completes. feeAmount is at least (amountIn + feeAmount) * swapFee / 1e6 in both branches of computeSwapStep (SwapMath.sol:72-74, 82 and 104) and swapFee is at least protocolFee (ProtocolFeeLibrary.sol:38-46), so the subtraction at Pool.sol:395 does not underflow. liquidityNet cannot be the minimum int128 because gross liquidity per tick is capped below 2^127 for every allowed spacing, about 2^108 at spacing 1 and 2^122 at spacing 32767 (Pool.sol:165-173 and 565-582). "+N0,
  "src/libraries/Pool.sol:393")
C("Spearbit 5.4.11 (informational, fixed): zeroForOne was masked with 0xff in getSqrtPriceTarget and in the tick assignment.",
  "Present: the flag is masked with 1 (src/libraries/SwapMath.sol:33) and the tick assignment is plain Solidity (Pool.sol:430-432). "+NA10,
  "src/libraries/SwapMath.sol:33")
C("Spearbit 5.4.15 (informational, fixed) and ABDK CVF-116 (minor): a pool whose total swap fee is 100 percent cannot serve exact output swaps.",
  "The revert is kept and documented: src/libraries/Pool.sol:311-316 rejects a positive amountSpecified when the swap fee is at least MAX_SWAP_FEE, and the interface says so at IPoolManager.sol:117 and 213. Without it the division by MAX_SWAP_FEE - feePips at SwapMath.sol:104 would be a division by zero inside mulDiv, which also reverts (FullMath.sol:30). "+N0,
  "src/libraries/Pool.sol:311")
C("Spearbit 5.4.18 (informational, fixed) and ABDK CVF-20 and CVF-46 (moderate): missing memory-safe annotations and code that overwrote part of the free memory pointer.",
  "Closed. The transient libraries carry the annotation and touch only scratch space (CurrencyDelta.sol:11-15, CurrencyReserves.sol:16-37). The transfer and the position hash no longer write below the free pointer area (Currency.sol:55-80, Position.sol:54-66), and StateLibrary obtains the position hash from Position.calculatePositionKey (StateLibrary.sol:239). "+NC,
  "src/types/Currency.sol:57")

# ---------------- ABDK major ----------------
